<task id="214" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H8 handler full rewrite (H8-B semantics): container-CREATION only, container-TYPE creation retired as operator prereq per SPAARKE-SPE-CONTAINER-TYPE-TOPOLOGY.md §R5 (verified 403 accessDenied 2026-08-30 SESSION 20 Option A probe)</title>
    <phase>Post-Live-Fire remediation — H8 architectural rewrite driven by empirical §R5 verification</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies handler code (H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs + GraphContainerTypeProvisioner.cs + collaborators — 700+ LOC in Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core), rewrites test surface (tests/unit/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core.Tests/Handlers/SpeContainerType/**), touches DagAdvancer.cs, KV manifest, potentially SKILL.md. Multiple hot-path surfaces per root CLAUDE.md §10. bff-api-adjacent per L2 control-plane. Main-session-only per §3 for any .claude/** edits.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-scoped mechanical rewrite: change of scope from container-type creation to container creation is a straightforward Graph SDK swap (Storage.FileStorage.ContainerTypes.PostAsync → Storage.FileStorage.Containers.PostAsync + activate). Interface refactoring is well-understood. Trap inversion is a mechanical delete. No architectural judgment beyond what topology doc §6 already dictates for container-creation flow. Sonnet 5 at xhigh handles this cleanly.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>H8 handler proper: ~4h (delete container-type creation code, rewrite as container-creation, update parameter guards). GraphContainerProvisioner rewrite: ~2h (new POST body shape, new activation call, new outcome shape). Interface refactoring (SpeContainerType* → SpeContainer*): ~1.5h. Test surface rewrite (~15 test files touching SpeContainerType*): ~3-4h — the biggest single time sink. KV manifest update (SPE-ContainerTypeId slot semantics): ~30 min. DagAdvancer + HandlerIds comment updates: ~15 min. Incidental cert-drift cleanup (retire spe-app-cert + spe-app-cert-pass from KV): ~30 min. Total 12-13h at xhigh. POML 213 original estimate 4h was based on "rename + swap" scope; empirical + drift findings pushed it to full rewrite.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>199, 212, 213</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, spe, h8, handler-rewrite, adr-028, topology-driven, bff-adjacent</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12h xhigh (H8 rewrite + provisioner rewrite + interface refactor + test surface rewrite + KV manifest + DagAdvancer + incidental cert-drift cleanup)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Task 213.2's Option A live-test empirically verified topology doc §R5 for the third time (topology doc §7 verified twice 2026-08-28 in sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2; we re-verified 2026-08-30 from r1 worktree). `client_credentials` grant against `POST /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes` returns **HTTP 403 accessDenied** regardless of credential shape (secret verified today; cert verified in topology doc). Grant-type is what matters (app-only vs delegated) per Microsoft OAuth semantics — credential shape (secret / cert / FIC) is irrelevant.

**Consequence**: H8SpeContainerTypeHandler as written cannot succeed against real Graph. Container-TYPE creation MUST become a one-time operator prereq (per SPAARKE-SPE-TOPOLOGY-SETUP-RUNBOOK.md Steps 1-3 filed by task 213.5). H8's remaining role at customer dispatch is container-CREATION only.

**Empirical evidence artifact**: [`runs/h8-live-test-2026-08-30.md`](../../../runs/h8-live-test-2026-08-30.md) — full probe methodology, response bodies, cert-drift finding, interpretation.

**Scope of task 214** (7 discrete work-items):

**214.1 — Delete container-TYPE creation code from GraphContainerTypeProvisioner.cs (~2h)**:
- File currently makes `graph.Storage.FileStorage.ContainerTypes.PostAsync(...)` call — DELETE that code path
- Also deletes owning-app permission-grant registration on containerTypeRegistrations (that call succeeds but is now redundant — done during operator runbook step 6)
- Only the container-creation code path survives — moved to new `GraphContainerProvisioner.cs` (renamed per 214.3 below)

**214.2 — Refactor H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs → H8SpeContainerHandler.cs (~4h)**:
- Rename file + class + HandlerIdentifier constant
- New responsibilities:
  - Read `containerTypeId` from `IntakeParameters.NonSecretParameters["containerTypeId"]` — populated by SKILL Step 4.0 payload construction from `spaarke-constants.yaml per_env_constants.<env>.containerTypeId` (populated by task 213.7 after operator completes runbook)
  - Read customer's `displayName` from `IntakeParameters.NonSecretParameters["customerId"]` (or a dedicated `containerDisplayName` intake field — decide during implementation)
  - Call `graph.Storage.FileStorage.Containers.PostAsync(new FileStorageContainer { DisplayName, Description, ContainerTypeId })` — this is the app-only-OK call per topology doc §6
  - Call `graph.Storage.FileStorage.Containers[{id}].Activate.PostAsync()` — container isn't usable until activated per §6
  - Persist the new container's GUID to `run.InterStepState.SpeContainerId` (H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler reads this to write to Dataverse env-var sprk_SharePointEmbeddedContainerId — unchanged handoff mechanism per H8 old code deviation-(2) note)
- Delete the KV write for `SPE-ContainerTypeId` — that value is now sourced from constants, not written per-customer
- Rebuild parameter guards for the new inputs (containerTypeId + displayName instead of tenantId + keyVaultName + subscriptionId + sharePointDomain + owningAppId — most of the old ones become moot)

**214.3 — Rename SpeContainerType* interfaces + collaborators → SpeContainer* (~1.5h)**:
- `ISpeContainerTypeProvisioner` → `ISpeContainerProvisioner`
- `ISpeContainerVerifier` — keep name; verification of the customer container remains conceptually similar (T6 gate becomes T6-relaxed since we're not creating container-types anymore, but verification-that-container-exists is still meaningful for H13 acceptance)
- `ISpeContainerIdKvWriter` — DELETE (per 214.2, no more KV write; containerTypeId comes from constants)
- `SpeContainerTypeOptions` → `SpeContainerOptions` (rename); trim fields that are now moot (`DefaultCertSecretName` may still be needed for the verifier — decide during implementation)
- `SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory` — KEEP for now if verifier still uses cert-based auth; DELETE if verifier is refactored to app-only (which is fine per topology doc §6 — verification via app-only is standard)
- Namespace `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Handlers.SpeContainerType` → `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Handlers.SpeContainer` (drop "Type" from folder name too)

**214.4 — Invert or delete T6 trap detection (~1h)**:
- `IsDelegatedTokenTrap` was designed for the INVERSE failure mode (assumed delegated returns 403, use confidential-client). Reality per §R5: confidential-client (client_credentials, regardless of secret/cert) returns 403 for container-TYPE creation; delegated is required. For container CREATION (§6), app-only is fine.
- Since H8's new shape doesn't create container-types at all, the T6 trap conceptually doesn't apply. Options:
  - **Option A (recommended)**: DELETE the T6 trap wiring entirely from H8's new shape. Keep the trap-code in the codebase as `SpeConfidentialClientGraphFactory.IsDelegatedTokenTrapError` for the H13 verifier's use only (T6 acceptance gate at H13). Document that H8 no longer participates in T6 detection.
  - **Option B**: keep T6 in H8 as a defense-in-depth check for any future re-introduction of container-type creation. Would fire never in practice (H8's new shape never hits the trap surface). Adds noise.
- Choose Option A. Update `SpeContainerTypeRejectionCodes.TrapT6DelegatedTokenDetected` — either remove or repurpose. H13's `TrapT6Failed` rejection code stays (H13 still owns T6 acceptance gate).

**214.5 — Rewrite test surface (~3-4h)**:
- All tests under `tests/unit/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core.Tests/Handlers/SpeContainerType/**` need review:
  - Tests that assert container-type creation success → DELETE (behavior no longer exists in H8)
  - Tests that assert T6 trap detection at H8 → DELETE per 214.4
  - Tests that assert KV write of SPE-ContainerTypeId → DELETE per 214.2
  - Tests that assert idempotency → REWRITE for new key shape (may become `container-{customerId}` since one container per customer)
  - Tests that assert parameter guards → REWRITE for new parameter set
  - NEW: tests that assert container CREATE + activate happy path
  - NEW: tests that assert containerTypeId param guard (missing → Resumable Failure)
  - NEW: tests that assert 24h replication tolerance if container-type just created (edge case — Cosmos WaitingOnGate + resume)

**214.6 — Update HandlerIds.cs + DagAdvancer.cs comments (~15 min)**:
- `HandlerIds.H8` — the ID string may encode "ContainerType" (verify + update if so)
- `DagAdvancer.cs:166` — update comment "H8 is Graph-based SPE container-type creation" → "H8 is Graph-based SPE container CREATION (per-customer; container-type is pre-existing per-model operator prereq)"
- H8's DAG dependency on H3 (Entra app-reg): review if still needed. New H8 doesn't need owningAppId from H3 (uses constants-sourced containerTypeId whose owning app is a topology prereq). Likely can REMOVE the H3 dep + rewire the DAG (would let H8 run earlier in parallel).

**214.7 — Incidental: retire KV cert drift (~30 min)**:
- KV `spaarke-spekvcert/spe-app-cert` (thumbprint `269691A5...`, CN=SPE Certificate 22Sept2025_1) is NOT registered on any Spaarke app-reg. It's dead weight (see runs/h8-live-test-2026-08-30.md incidental finding).
- Options: (a) retire (soft-delete both secrets — cert + password); (b) register the cert on SDAP-PCF-CLIENT to fix drift (unnecessary if H8's new shape doesn't need it).
- Choose (a). Also update `spe-owning-app-secret` slot: retain per topology doc §3A row 1 for the owning app rotation lifecycle (E-1 exception per ADR-028) — do NOT retire that one.
- **Cross-reference to KV credential-lifecycle rule** in `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md`: `spe-app-cert` + `spe-app-cert-pass` are NOT in the never-delete list (unlike `Dataverse-ClientSecret` + `BFF-API-ClientSecret` which have specific auth-v4 governance). They are ordinary application secrets and can be retired when confirmed unused.
- Verify via git grep that no code path references either secret name before retiring.

**Sequencing constraint**: 214 can proceed in PARALLEL with 213.4 (Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 extension) — different files touched. 214 does NOT depend on operator completing the runbook setup (that's 213.7's dependency). Task 186 dispatch blocks on {213.4, 213.7, 214, 207, 208, 209}.

**Reference architecture** (topology doc §6 canonical container creation shape):
```http
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/beta/storage/fileStorage/containers
Authorization: Bearer <app-only Graph token; grant_type=client_credentials — WORKS for container creation, unlike container-TYPE creation>
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Acme Corp", "description": "Container for Acme Corp trial customer", "containerTypeId": "{containerTypeId from constants}" }

POST /beta/storage/fileStorage/containers/{newContainerId}/activate
```

Deletion for tests / dev cleanup follows §6 two-step:
```http
DELETE /beta/storage/fileStorage/containers/{id}
DELETE /beta/storage/fileStorage/deletedContainers/{id}
```</prompt>

  <role>Main-session operator (skill-directives + BFF-adjacent handler code + test rewrite + KV governance).</role>

  <goal>H8 handler is renamed + reworked to CREATE containers (not container-types) per topology doc §6. Container-TYPE creation is retired from the handler codebase — it exists only in the operator runbook (task 213.5). All tests updated; DagAdvancer updated; KV manifest updated; cert drift cleanup landed. Trial1 dispatch progresses through H8 successfully (creates trial1's container inside the pre-existing Spaarke Trial 1 container-type).</goal>

