  <constraints>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-R1">Container-type owning app is PERMANENT + 1:1 with container-type. H8's new shape MUST NOT attempt to create container-types (per this task's verified §R5 basis). Container-type creation is retired to operator runbook (task 213.5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-R5">Container-type CREATE requires delegated token. H8 uses app-only per its runtime environment (L2 control-plane UAMI-federated identity or similar). H8 MUST NOT attempt container-type creation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="topology-doc-6">Container creation (`POST /storage/fileStorage/containers` + activate) is app-only-capable. This is H8's new scope. Follow-up `/activate` is REQUIRED — container isn't usable until activated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028-A4">BFF identity is secret-free. Do NOT introduce any `.WithClientSecret(...)` site on the BFF identity in H8's new shape. Verifier's cert-based auth (if retained per 214.3) uses the owning app's cert per E-1 exception, NOT the BFF identity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE-md-3">Sub-Agent Write Boundary — SKILL.md edits main-session-only. Handler code + tests are inside src/**/tests/** which sub-agents CAN write, but this task is FULL rigor + interconnected so main-session is expected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="kv-credential-lifecycle">spe-app-cert + spe-app-cert-pass are NOT in the never-delete list (unlike Dataverse-ClientSecret + BFF-API-ClientSecret which are auth-v4-governed). Retire only after git grep verifies no code path references them.</constraint>
  </constraints>

